=== HOW TO READ THIS
  The rejection counters are CUMULATIVE OVER THE WHOLE SOLVE, trials included, so
  their absolute values carry the search's history. Only the DIFFERENCES between
  consecutive rows belong to the final march, and only those should be read.
  If a difference is zero across an interval in which the front moved, then the
  locator neither accepted nor refused anything there -- which would mean it was
  not called at all, and the question moves to why.
